/**
 * @page HanNodeDeviceLibrary HAN IoT Shield Support Library
 *
 * @brief Hardware abstraction layer for the HAN IoT prototype shield.
 *
 * This library provides a hardware abstraction layer for the
 * HAN IoT prototype shield used during development of the
 * rainwater monitoring prototype.
 *
 * 
 * The library isolates all shield-specific pin assignments,
 * input handling and LED control functionality from the
 * application logic. As a result, the application code can
 * access shield resources through a simple and consistent
 * interface without depending on physical pin numbers.
 *
 *
 * @section Purpose Purpose
 *
 * The library has two main responsibilities:
 *
 * - Initializing the hardware available on the prototype shield.
 * - Reading user inputs and controlling visual feedback LEDs.
 *
 * The library therefore acts as the interface between the
 * application software and the development hardware.
 *
 *
 * @section ShieldResources Supported Shield Resources
 *
 * The library provides access to:
 *
 * - Four LEDs.
 * - Two push buttons.
 * - Two potentiometers.
 * - A OneWire interface for Dallas temperature sensors.
 *
 * During prototype development the potentiometers and push
 * buttons are used to emulate physical sensors.
 *
 * @section Calling Calling the library
 *
 * @code
 * #include "hanNodeDevice.h"
 * @endcode
 *
 * The library's files are parts of the prototype LoraWAN Node application
 *
 *
 * @section Initialization Hardware Initialization
 *
 * The function:
 *
 * @code
 * initializeNodeHardware()
 * @endcode
 *
 * configures all required GPIO pins and prepares the
 * prototype shield for operation.
 *
 *
 * @section RuntimeOperation Runtime Operation
 *
 * During normal operation the application periodically calls:
 *
 * @code
 * ledsControl()
 * @endcode
 *
 * This function:
 *
 * - Reads the state of the push buttons.
 * - Reads the potentiometer values.
 * - Updates the LED brightness.
 * - Updates globally available hardware status variables.
 *
 *
 * @section RelationToPrototype Relation to the Prototype
 *
 * The rainwater monitoring application uses this library for:
 *
 * - Flow meter pulse simulation through the red push button.
 * - Battery voltage simulation through the red potentiometer.
 * - Water level simulation through the white potentiometer.
 * - User feedback through the shield LEDs.
 *
 *
 * @section HANIoTLibrary HAN IoT Shield Library
 *
 * An alternative to this support library is the HAN IoT Shield
 * library designed by Remko Welling, which can be installed through the
 * <b>Library Manager</b> in the Arduino IDE.
 *
 * The HAN IoT Shield library provides a higher-level interface
 * to the hardware available on the prototype shield, including:
 *
 * - LEDs
 * - Push buttons
 * - Potentiometers
 * - Dallas temperature sensor support
 *
 * Using the HAN IoT Shield library simplifies application
 * development by providing easy access to shield functionality
 * without requiring direct manipulation of GPIO pins.
 *
 * The support library described on this page was developed to
 * provide a lightweight hardware abstraction layer tailored to
 * the requirements of this project. Future developments may
 * choose either approach depending on the desired level of
 * abstraction and functionality.
 *
 *
 *
 * @see ShieldLayout
 * @see ApplicationArchitecture
 */